# What the host has no business serving.
#
# On GitHub Pages every one of these was downloadable: alprojects.co/endpoint/
# form.php returned 200 with the PHP in plain text, and so did
# tools/build-pages.py. The endpoint is the one that matters -- it is the file
# that will hold a mail configuration, and the standing rule that it must never
# carry a key exists precisely because the host served it. The rule stays, and
# now the host does not serve it either.
#
# None of this is referenced by any page: checked across every built HTML file
# for href, src, srcset and action pointing at these directories.
tools/
content/
endpoint/
README.md
.github/

# GitHub Pages read this to learn the custom domain. Vercel takes the domain
# from the project, so the file is only history here -- kept in the repository
# until Pages is switched off, not shipped to the host.
CNAME

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
.gitignore
vercel.json
.vercelignore
